[{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer. CI passed.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `test_half_even` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't confirm what it requires. The fix is based on the test and the docstring.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}